356 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/A 357 0 R/Alt(The flow chart outlines a step-by-step process for running predictions on image tiles. It begins with listing all JPEG files in a directory, then checks if there are more tiles to process. If no tiles remain, the process ends. If tiles remain, the next tile is read, and an initial prediction is made using a first model to get valid bounding boxes. These boxes are refined through predictions with a second and then a third model, adding detections while avoiding duplicates. The final bounding boxes are saved in a dictionary. Arrows show the sequence and decision points, with a clear "No" path leading to the end and a "Yes" path continuing the loop. This diagram helps understand how multiple models work together to refine image detection results across multiple tiles.\000)/K[2]/S/Figure/P 81 0 R/Pg 11 0 R>>
endobj

